# ESLint Pre-Commit Compliance (BBB HTML5)

Husky runs `eslint` on staged `*.{js,jsx,ts,tsx}` and `tsc --noEmit --incremental` (`tscheck:staged`) before every commit. **Errors block the commit**; fix them before finishing work.

## Before Committing

```bash
cd bigbluebutton-html5
npx eslint path/to/changed/file.tsx
npm run tscheck:staged   # or: npx tsc --noEmit --incremental
```

## Common Rules in This Project

### `react/jsx-indent` — child elements must align with parent depth

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — child at same indent as parent opening tag
<Styled.Message>
<Styled.HtmlContent />
</Styled.Message>

// ✅ GOOD — child indented 2 spaces inside parent
<Styled.Message>
  <Styled.HtmlContent />
</Styled.Message>
```

### `object-curly-newline` — multi-item imports/exports need line breaks

```js
// ❌ BAD — 4+ named imports on one line
import React, { useContext, useEffect, useMemo, useState } from 'react';

// ✅ GOOD
import React, {
  useContext, useEffect, useMemo, useState,
} from 'react';
```

### `react/prop-types` — warnings only (usually non-blocking)

Prefer matching existing file style. Do not add PropTypes to `.tsx` files that use TypeScript interfaces unless the file already uses PropTypes.

### TypeScript selectors in hooks — return type must match `Partial<T>`

```ts
// ❌ BAD — inline type narrows breakoutRoomsSummary incompatible with User
useCurrentUser((u: { breakoutRoomsSummary?: { totalOfJoinURL?: number } }) => ({
  breakoutRoomsSummary: u.breakoutRoomsSummary,
}));

// ✅ GOOD — let hook infer Partial<User>
useCurrentUser((u) => ({
  isModerator: u.isModerator,
  breakoutRoomsSummary: u.breakoutRoomsSummary,
}));
```

## Agent Checklist

When editing BBB frontend files:

1. Preserve JSX indentation — each nested element +2 spaces
2. Break long `{ a, b, c, d }` import/export braces across lines
3. Run `npx eslint` on touched files before telling the user work is done
4. If commit fails on pre-commit, fix errors and retry — never suggest `--no-verify`
